--[[
  Jurang Kelam — Delta script v2
  Runtime : Roblox / Luau, executor Delta (mobile friendly)
  Target  : PlaceId 116463962153167 (GameId 10770728771), the hub
  Source  : Dumper++ v5.0 dump, 2026-11-02, place version 167
  Run     : join the hub -> Execute -> panel appears (draggable, "-" minimizes).
            Re-executing unloads the previous copy first.
  Status  : written from the decompiled client scripts, NOT tested in-game.
            Anything marked (inferred) depends on a name the dump did not show live.

  What "level 1-10" means here: the game has 10 element categories
  (Connection, Light, Darkness, Fire, Earth, Water, Energy, Time, Ice, Air), 10 eggs each:
  eggs 1-5 Common, 6-9 Primal, 10 Mythic. Progress = eggs owned (x/100), zones discovered (x/10),
  NPC trades done (x/11).

  AUTO JOURNEY runs these steps in a loop (content is unlocked by the event schedule, so it
  re-checks every CFG.roundDelay seconds and does whatever is open):
   1 sweep    Visits waypoints (TeleTargetAttachment tag + zone portals) so the map streams in, and
              collects every egg/UGC drop it finds. Drops are Parts with a "PickUp" RemoteEvent; the
              game fires PickUp itself when the 5-stud ProximityPrompt shows, we fire it as a fallback.
   2 zones    EggIntoPortal parts (attr CategoryIndex + child CamLook). We stand on the portal and let the
              game's own cutscene finish (it sets PlayedEggIntoPortal<N> and fires DiscoveredZoneReward).
              If it never finishes we fire DiscoveredZoneReward(portal) ourselves.
   3 trades   TradeNPC parts (attr TradeListIndex). Trade i (1-10): 5 spare Common eggs -> 1 Primal of
              category i, trade 11: any Primal. Limit 1 each (player attr qf_NPCTrade<i>). The game only
              lets you offer duplicates (amount-1 per egg) and lets you pick the reward, so we offer
              spare commons and pick the Primal we own the fewest of.
              Call: NPCTrade:FireServer(tradeId, {["cat"]={["idx"]=n}}, {cat, idx}) - same as the GUI.
   4 gifts    Gift spawns show an "Insert Tokens" prompt; triggering it makes the game insert a token while
              SpentTokens < EarnedTokens (Elite: SpentEliteTokens / EarnedEliteTokens).
  Not automated on purpose: the Final Exit portal (it leaves the hub) and anything the server
  gates by time (EventDay / Gate3) - those open when the schedule says so.
]]

